{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PEAK-WINDOW PAUSE acknowledged (operator-ordered, 5-11am PT). Checked the clock at 04:52 PT;\nmy next action was a PUSH, so I am standing down rather than racing the window. Nothing was\nsubmitted and nothing was pushed. Recording state for the resume order.\n\n## STOP — do NOT submit 1727 as it currently stands on Gerrit\n\nChange 1727 shows LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1, so it LOOKS ready. It is not. Those votes are\non revision f34549d099, which PREDATES the five advisory fixes from its own review round. That\nrevision still contains the defect the review found:\n\n  `run_sweep` stamps the last-sweep clock in its `finally`, INCLUDING when it stood aside\n  because the store lock was busy. A stand-aside folds nothing, so stamping it suppresses the\n  staleness arm for a full interval. Under sustained contention every trigger stands aside,\n  stamps, and goes quiet — the store never compacts while looking freshly swept. That is worse\n  than shipping no floor at all, because the signal claims it is working.\n\nSubmitting 1727 as-is would land exactly that. The corrected commit is 8bfe41b9e2 and it is\nLOCAL ONLY — pushing it is the prohibited action, which is why the fix is not on Gerrit yet.\n\n## State at standdown\n\nGerrit:\n- 1717 — status NEW, LLM-Review +1, Verified PENDING, revision 3cfde6b8f3 (\"Sweep compaction\n  out of band on a schedule\"). CI may finish on its own during the window; that is fine.\n- 1727 — status NEW, LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, revision f34549d099 (\"Trigger compaction from\n  the close, out of band\"). STALE — see above.\n\nLocal, worktree /Users/joeoakhart/ray-close-lock, branch basilisk-sweep, working tree CLEAN:\n- 8bfe41b9e2  Trigger compaction from the close, out of band   <- has the 5 advisory fixes\n- 3cfde6b8f3  Sweep compaction out of band on a schedule        <- identical to 1717's revision\n- 6601e5fb21  (main) Guard caplog on the reconciler root too\n\nVerification of 8bfe41b9e2 so far: integration tier 194 passed / 1 skipped; ruff, mypy (526\nfiles), complexity ratchet unchanged, module-size contract, actionlint + zizmor all clean. The\nfull main tier was still running when the pause landed — I am not acting on its result either\nway, and the resume should treat it as unconfirmed and re-run it.\n\n## Resume checklist (~11am PT)\n\n1. In the worktree above, re-run the main tier on 8bfe41b9e2 and confirm green.\n2. `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main` — updates 1727 to a new patch set (RESETTING its\n   current votes, which is correct: they certify the wrong code). 1717's commit is unchanged,\n   so it gets no new patch set.\n3. Wait for LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1 on the NEW 1727 patch set, and for 1717's Verified.\n4. Submit the TOP of the stack (1727); Gerrit carries its ancestor 1717 with it.\n5. Realign the worktree to the merged tip via the gerrit remote, tick the ACs, and close\n   gaudy-gangrenous-basilisk.\n\nThe ticket stays in_progress and must NOT close before both land — per the standing constraint\nthat it may not close with the CI-less gap open. Story A (choosy-arthrodic-barbet) is already\nclosed and merged as 04b78f5e7e; only the sweep and the operation-linked floor remain."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786622030186844001,"uuid":"5500fa1e-ac0e-4cce-bcf5-e2ce9f0fcdb4"}